 added element which  makes this a reliable technique  as headshots are the fabled crit area  jumping and shooting down on an opponent  with a shotgun stacks the odds of a  headshot in your favor  I'm absolutely terrible at it and prefer  boots on the ground but anyone who plays  the recent Call of Duty titles titanfall  Orem lawbreakers will be able to use  this strategy with ease here's an  example when this chap is jumping around  my aim is all over the place but as soon  as he's back on the ground I can  absolutely melt him a minor tip I  believe is worth mentioning happened  right at the start of the game when  jumping out from the party bus your  glider or umbrella will pop at a certain  distance from the ground but it will  activate earlier if it's above mountains  buildings or trees if you want to get to  the ground quicker drop above ravines  low level areas or skirt the island  shoreline is an example when going for a  loop lake I tend to jump later than  everyone else and aim for the stream or  in between the hills then when my  umbrella pops I slice through the air  and reach the target first then  hopefully I've got to drop on other  players pistol there's also something to  be said about landing last whilst other  players are flying out of the bus like  misguided sperm I jumped out as late as  possible and glided all the way to the  ground and look almost half the  population were already dead and even  better than that I actually won that  game so first down on the ground isn't  always the best tactic next it's the  question to bait or kill when an enemy  is riddled full of bullets they fall to  the ground waiting for help from a  teammate in duels I highly recommend  using the downed enemy as bait to draw  out their partner in crime potentially  losing half your team causes that  last-man-standing to push forward to  save their fallen comrade and depending  on how they approach it two against one  they haven't got  it's easy enough in squads I recommend  the opposite surprisingly using a force  bait can be highly advantageous don't  get me wrong but the risk/reward doesn't  quite stack up in my opinion once our  squad started killing those stragglers  outright the opposition began running in  like mad dogs I actually understand this  mentality too if you are playing as a  group of four friends and lose a man or  two early on your odds of winning are  cut dramatically and your death friends  are stuck watching instead of playing  many teams will go on a kamikaze mission  me included two off one of the  Opposition squad as soon as possible  so do you bait or do you motorized I'd  love to know what your preference is  let's talk about reviving far too often  the building mechanic is completely  ignored in Battle Royale  most probably by those of us who started  out in player and notes battlegrounds  when a teammate hits the deck build a  shelter around them to both protect and  obscure the opposition's line-of-sight  if they decide to rush you you can be  set with a shotgun if they keep their  distance get your buddy back in the game  and just don't do what I did and  accidentally shoot your pal in the head  if you're watching hands  I'm so sorry fella it won't happen again  another underutilized building  opportunity is when you are looting a  corpse instinct usually takes over here  and we dart in grab gear and hopefully  get away quickly well a huge amount of  kills happen when people are looting  once again build around those goodies  and keep yourself and your team safe if  you remember my tactic from earlier I  actively use dropped weapons and other  Desirables to entice the opposition to  come over and then I ambush those new  book as soon dude another one bites the  dust have you ever tried to pick up  resources and accidentally pick up  weapons instead  well this mechanic will soon be changed  allowing us to walk through the drops to  instantly pick up materials and  consumables in the meantime though if 